{"id":"n1-106","title":"Noun を皮切りにして","romaji":"Noun wo kawakiri ni shite","jlptLevel":1,"shortExplanation":"Used to express 'Starting with', 'Beginning with'","longExplanation":"'Noun を皮切りにして' is a Japanese grammatical form used when one wants to express that something begins with a certain event or action, then continues on in a sequence. It is the same as saying 'starting with...' or 'beginning with...' in English.","formation":"Noun + を皮切りに (して)","examples":[{"jp":"彼はその日を皮切りにして毎日ジムに通い始めました。","romaji":"Kare wa sono hi o kawakiri ni shite mainichi jimu ni kayoi hajimemashita.","en":"Starting from that day, he began to go to the gym every day.","words":[{"surface":"彼","vocabId":"1483070","reading":"かれ"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"その","vocabId":null},{"surface":"日","vocabId":"1463770","reading":"ひ"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"皮切り","vocabId":"1483880","reading":"かわきり"},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"し","vocabId":"1310720","reading":"し","baseForm":"する"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"毎日","vocabId":"1524720","reading":"まいにち"},{"surface":"ジム","vocabId":"1314270","reading":"じむ"},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"通い","vocabId":"1636730","reading":"かよい","baseForm":"通う"},{"surface":"始め","vocabId":"1342540","reading":"はじめ","baseForm":"始める"},{"surface":"まし","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"ます"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[4,5,6]},{"jp":"新年会を皮切りにして、今年はたくさんのイベントが開催されます。","romaji":"Shinnenkai o kawakiri ni shite, kotoshi wa takusan no ibento ga kaisai saremasu.","en":"Starting with the New Year's party, a lot of events will be held this year.","words":[{"surface":"新年","vocabId":"1362290","reading":"しんねん"},{"surface":"会","vocabId":"1198160","reading":"え"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"皮切り","vocabId":"1483880","reading":"かわきり"},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"し","vocabId":"1310720","reading":"し","baseForm":"する"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},